The Cybersecurity Policy Simplifier is a generative AI application built on AWS PartyRock (powered by Amazon Bedrock). It solves a critical compliance and GRC (Governance, Risk, and Compliance) problem: security policies are often written in dense legal and technical jargon, making them difficult for general employees, executives, and IT staff to understand and follow.
This tool ingests raw policy text and outputs a plain-language version, role-specific guidance, an actionable Do/Don't list, and a comprehension quiz, all while maintaining strict AI guardrails to prevent hallucination and policy drift.
✨ Key Features
•	Multi-Level Translation: Adapts policy language to specific reading levels (Grade 8, Grade 10, Professional).
•	Role-Based Guidance: Generates tailored "What this means for me" sections for different audiences (Employees, Executives, IT, Contractors).
•	Zero-Hallucination Guardrails: Uses prompt engineering to explicitly flag ambiguous text [AMBIGUOUS: ...] or missing clauses [POLICY IS SILENT ON: ...] rather than inventing rules.
•	Fidelity Audit (QA Layer): Automatically compares the generated plain-language version against the original text to flag any dropped, weakened, or altered requirements.
•	Automated Comprehension Check: Generates 4 scenario-based multiple-choice questions strictly derived from the generated obligations.


🏗️ Architecture & Workflow
This app uses a sequential AI chaining architecture. The output of one widget becomes the context for the next, creating a robust data pipeline:
1.	Input: PolicyText (Paragraph), ReadingLevel (Dropdown), TargetAudience (Dropdown), KeepMandatory (Checkbox).
2.	Processing Engine 1 (PlainLanguagePolicy): Ingests raw text and applies plain-language rules. Temp: 0.2.
3.	Processing Engine 2 (RoleGuide): Ingests simplified text and tailors it to the selected audience. Temp: 0.3.
4.	Processing Engine 3 (DosAndDonts): Extracts exact obligations into a 5x5 list. Temp: 0.2.
5.	QA Engine (FidelityAudit): Compares Input vs. Output of Engine 1 to catch any lost requirements. Temp: 0.2.
6.	Training Engine (ComprehensionCheck): Generates a quiz based on Engine 3's output. Temp: 0.4.


🛠️ Tech Stack
